    "q-183349": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183349",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$\\,$ If $x\\in N,$ then  $x$ is positive.\n\nWhich of the following is logically equivalent to the conditional predicate above?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ the following predicates:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x\\in N.$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is positive.\n\nThen, our initial sentence can be written as $P(x)⇒Q(x),$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬P(x)∨Q(x).\n$$\n\nThe negation of $P(x)$ can be written as\n\n- $¬P(x):$ $x\\notin N.$\n\nTherefore, the given sentence is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ $x\\notin N,$ or $x$ is positive.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-183349-a",
